---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { COMPANY_NAME, COMPANY_LOCATION } from '../data/company';
import { SUPPORTER_DISCLOSURE, SUPPORTER_REWARD } from '../data/commerce';

const TERMS_VERSION = '2026-08-26';
---

<Layout
  title="Founder Supporter Pack terms | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Terms for the ByteLite LLC Founder Supporter Pack: a one-time commercial purchase with a defined digital reward. Not a donation and not tax deductible."
  keywords="ByteLite Founder Supporter Pack terms"
  canonical="https://www.thebytelite.com/supporter-terms/"
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="draft">DRAFT &mdash; awaiting owner review. Not legal or tax advice.</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Founder Supporter Pack terms</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Version {TERMS_VERSION}. {COMPANY_NAME}, {COMPANY_LOCATION}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="disclosure">
        <p>{SUPPORTER_DISCLOSURE}</p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt">1. What this is.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        A one-time purchase of digital goods from {COMPANY_NAME}, a for-profit Montana limited
        liability company. You choose the amount you pay at checkout. It is not recurring and will
        never renew.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">2. What you receive.</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        {SUPPORTER_REWARD.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="body">
        That list is exhaustive. Nothing outside it is part of this purchase.
      </p>
      <p class="body warn">
        <strong>Open item:</strong> the exact reward files have not been finalised. The purchase
        control stays disabled until they exist, so nobody can buy a pack that cannot be delivered.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">3. What this is not.</h2>
      <p class="body">This purchase does not give you:</p>
      <ul class="list list-no">
        <li>a charitable donation or any tax deduction &mdash; ByteLite LLC is a for-profit company;</li>
        <li>equity, shares, options, voting rights or any ownership interest;</li>
        <li>repayment, interest, revenue share or profit participation;</li>
        <li>an investment, or any expectation of financial return;</li>
        <li>ownership of, or a licence to, ByteLite LLC intellectual property;</li>
        <li>access to ByteLite, Cordel Connect, Cordel Play or any future product;</li>
        <li>early or beta software access;</li>
        <li>any control over, or say in, what gets developed;</li>
        <li>a promise that any particular feature, product, capability or date will be delivered.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt">4. The supporter wall.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Inclusion is optional and off by default. It happens only if you tick a separate, unticked
        box and choose a display name. That consent is separate from your purchase consent and from
        any marketing consent &mdash; agreeing to one is never agreeing to another.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        To be removed, ask through the <a href="/contact">privacy contact</a>. Removal does not
        refund the purchase, because the digital reward has already been delivered.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">5. Refunds.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        The reward is digital and delivered immediately on payment. If the files are not delivered,
        or are not what this page describes, contact me and I will refund you in full. If you
        received what is listed in section 2, the purchase is complete.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">6. Payment and data.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Payment is handled by Stripe. ByteLite LLC never receives or stores your card number. What
        is retained is the fact of the purchase, the plan key and the terms version, so the reward
        can be delivered and the transaction can be accounted for. See the
        <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">7. Tax.</h2>
      <p class="body warn">
        <strong>Open item:</strong> this is a taxable commercial sale, not a gift. Whether sales
        tax applies to you depends on registrations and product tax codes that are not yet
        configured. That is a decision for a qualified tax professional, not for this page, and the
        purchase control stays disabled until it is settled.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
.narrow { max-width: 780px; }
.page-hero { padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; }
.draft {
  display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase;
  color: #fbbf24; background: rgba(251,191,36,.08); border: 1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.3);
  border-radius: 9999px; padding: .3rem .875rem;
}
.hero-sub { max-width: 640px; font-size: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.8; }
h2 { margin-bottom: .75rem; font-size: 1.125rem; }
.mt { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
.body { font-size: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem; }
.warn {
  background: rgba(251,191,36,.06); border: 1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.28);
  border-radius: .5rem; padding: 1rem; color: #c4c8f0;
}
.disclosure {
  padding: 1.25rem; background: rgba(244,114,182,.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(244,114,182,.3); border-radius: .625rem;
}
.disclosure p { font-size: .9375rem; color: #f0d0e0; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
.list { list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: .5rem; }
.list li {
  font-size: .9375rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.65;
  padding: .625rem .875rem; background: #0d1120;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #34d399; border-radius: .5rem;
}
.list-no li { border-left-color: #f472b6; }
</style>
